        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.105,
            0.899,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "MATHEMATICS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.138,
            0.901,
            0.174
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) The product of two consecutive positive integers is 306. We need to find the integers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.179,
            0.9,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Rohan’s mother is 26 years older than him. The product of their ages (in years) 3 years from now will be 360. We would like to find Rohan’s present age."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.221,
            0.901,
            0.274
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) A train travels a distance of 480 km at a uniform speed. If the speed had been 8 km/h less, then it would have taken 3 hours more to cover the same distance. We need to find the speed of the train."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.286,
            0.675,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.3 Solution of a Quadratic Equation by Factorisation"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.313,
            0.902,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider the quadratic equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2x^{2} - 3x + 1 = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If we replace x by 1 on the LHS of this equation, we get "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(2 \\times 1^{2}) - (3 \\times 1) + 1 = 0 =  RHS"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the equation. We say that 1 is a root of the quadratic equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2x^{2} - 3x + 1 = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . This also means that 1 is a zero of the quadratic polynomial "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 x ^ { 2 } - 3 x + 1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.397,
            0.902,
            0.494
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In general, a real number   is called a root of the quadratic equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax^{2}+bx+c=0, a \\neq 0   if   a \\alpha^{2}+b\\alpha+c=0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . We also say that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = \\mathbf{a}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "is a solution of",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the quadratic equation, or that   "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "satisfies the quadratic equation",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Note that "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "the",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " zeroes of the quadratic polynomial "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax^{2} + bx + c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "and the roots of the quadratic",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax^{2} + bx + c = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "are the same",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.499,
            0.901,
            0.538
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You have observed, in Chapter 2, that a quadratic polynomial can have at most two zeroes. So, any quadratic equation can have atmost two roots."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.543,
            0.902,
            0.602
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You have learnt in Class IX, how to factorise quadratic polynomials by splitting their middle terms. We shall use this knowledge for finding the roots of a quadratic equation. Let us see how."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.614,
            0.835,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 3 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find the roots of the equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2x^{2} - 5x + 3 = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , by factorisation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.64,
            0.9,
            0.678
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let us first split the middle term – 5x as –2x –3x [because "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(-2x) \\times (-3x) ="
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 x ^ { 2 } = ( 2 x ^ { 2 } ) \\times 3 ]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.683,
            0.841,
            0.703
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2x^{2}-5x+3=2x^{2}-2x-3x+3=2x(x-1)-3(x-1)=(2x-3)(x-1)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.709,
            0.691,
            0.728
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2x^{2} - 5x + 3 = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " can be rewritten as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(2x - 3)(x - 1) = 0."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.734,
            0.898,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the values of x for which "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2x^{2} - 5x + 3 = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are the same for which "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 2 x - 3 ) ( x - 1 ) = 0 ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " i.e., either "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2x - 3 = 0   or   x - 1 = 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.775,
            0.626,
            0.813
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2x - 3 = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " gives "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x   =   \\frac { 3 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x - 1 = 0 \\;  gives  \\; x = 1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.809,
            0.608,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x   =   \\frac { 3 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are the solutions of the equation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.84,
            0.773,
            0.879
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In other words, 1 and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are the roots of the equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2x^{2} - 5x + 3 = 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.967,
            0.563,
            0.982
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.88,
            0.601,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Verify",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " that these are the roots of the given equation."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
